- Progress-scope rule: each `AGENT_PROGRESS.md` records only changes to state inside its own folder. When a nested subfolder carries its own four-file agent contract, this folder logs only the event of creating or removing that nested workspace plus parent-owned coordination, blocker, or decision state; later child-internal changes (design edits, corpus additions, rename cascades, blocker updates) live in the nested `AGENT_PROGRESS.md` and are not duplicated here. Cross-child coordination belongs in parent progress; sibling-internal facts belong in the corresponding child progress. The same applies symmetrically: a nested workspace's progress file does not restate parent-scope events.
